    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d574">

                <pb facs="0758" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg750"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/1071a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Thurston</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at Kuibyshev</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-13T15:00:00-05:00">December 13,
                            1941—3 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1284. 1. The Military Attaché in London has informed us that he has learned from
                    an excellent source that Sikorski<anchor n="54" xml:id="d574-f1"/> while in the
                    Soviet Union has informed Stalin that he is of the opinion that the Soviet Union
                    should not enter the war with Japan and that he does not believe that the
                    Japanese unless forced so to do will attack the Soviet Union. The Military
                    Attaché also reports that he has learned that Sir Stafford Cripps<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d574-f2"/> agrees in this matter with Sikorski.</p>
                <p>2. Any information which you may be able discreetly to obtain which might tend to
                    confirm or refute this information would be helpful.</p>
                <pb facs="0759" n="751" xml:id="pg751"/>
                <p>3. [Here follows report of conversation with the Soviet Ambassador, recorded in
                    memorandum by the Secretary of State December 11, printed on <ref
                        target="#pg742">page 742</ref>.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d574-f1" n="54" xml:id="d574-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. Wladyslaw Sikorski, Polish Prime Minister.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d574-f2" n="55" xml:id="d574-f2-content">
                <p>British Ambassador in the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
